-- title:
--   Finiteness of vertex stabilisers in the projective away-unit group
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be rational numbers with $a<0$ and $b<0$, so that $\mathbb{H} = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is a definite rational quaternion algebra, and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ satisfying `IsOrder R`, i.e. $1 \in R$, $R$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $R$ is all of $\mathbb{H}$, and $R$ is finitely generated. Let $v$ be a height one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$. Write $\Gamma :=$ `CosetGraph.awayUnits R v` for the subgroup of $\mathbb{H}^\times$ cut out as the infimum, over all height one primes $w \neq v$, of the preimages under `toLoc w` of the subgroup generated by [`Submodule.localBoxUnits R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45) in the units of the local algebra `Loc a b w`. This group acts on `CosetGraph.Vert R v`, the quotient of the unit group of `Loc a b v` by `CosetGraph.level R v`, the subgroup generated by [`Submodule.localBoxUnits R v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45) together with `scalarUnits v`; let `CosetGraph.ProjAwayUnits R v` be the quotient of $\Gamma$ by the kernel of the associated permutation representation on `CosetGraph.Vert R v`. The assertion is that for every $x$ in `CosetGraph.Vert R v` the stabiliser of $x$ in `CosetGraph.ProjAwayUnits R v` is a finite type.
--
--   This is the discreteness input for the action of the $v$-away unit group of an order in a definite rational quaternion algebra on the coset space at $v$ (the vertices of the Bruhat–Tits tree when the order is maximal and $v$ is a splitting place): stabilisers of vertices are finite because, after conjugation, they consist of units of an order in a definite algebra. It feeds the finiteness-and-finitely-many-orbits statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.evenAwayUnits_finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_exists_finset_orbits_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.evenAwayUnits_finite_stabilizer_vertex_and_exists_finset_orbits_of_not_dvd) in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset graph.
-- source:
